  "description": "NESJUT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C93 H93 O38 Tb7,7(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.579-3.924 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.46-111.73°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C107H114N7O38Tb7. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
